<div id="2026-09-05-hardware-monitor-silent-on-success" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-05 — Hardware monitor: silence success output to stop gateway cron emails</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Made <code>hardware_monitor.pl</code> produce zero stdout/stderr on success path (the two <code>print</code> statements that logged the exact "monitoring triggered via ... (HTTP 200)" and "logging audit triggered" lines were removed). The audit trigger still happens (curl still executed), just silently. Updated deploy cron setup to target <code>/tmp/comserv-hardware-monitor.log</code> (with mkdir/touch/chmod 666 for writability) instead of /var/log/.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> On the .03 gateway server (proxmoxt210 / 192.168.1.3 host-side cron only, no app code), the periodic success output from the script was being emailed (likely via cron MAILTO when the >> redirect to /var/log failed due to ownership/permissions for the crontab user). The real success signal lives in the <code>monitor_heartbeat</code> rows written by the app <code>/admin/hardware_monitor/run</code> endpoint. Outages still use the sole reliable channel (script STDERR → cron mail) when no node responds.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>script/hardware_monitor.pl</code>, <code>script/deploy.sh</code>, <code>root/Documentation/changelog/entries/2026-09-05-hardware-monitor-silent-on-success.inc</code></p>
</div>